I've had no problems running Nethack on WM5 WM6 and WM6.1.

What device are you using?  If it's a smartphone (WM Standard) then
you will run into problems running the binary designed for touch
screens (WM Professional).  A locked smartphone will have problems
running unsigned code (the Nethack binary is unsigned AFAIK).  There
is an experimental version of Nethack designed to run on Smartphones.
Check the Nethack distro page.

Also, make sure that you are aren't trying to execute a version for a
different type of CE device.  WinCE 5.0 devices are not really Pocket
PC's (although the PPC OS is based on CE5.0).  Running the HPC version
will give you error you described above.


